think HUNK60 turned a drag into a .crop edit that lived only in numbers; the crop gesture's visible half was still missing. Took HUNK61 — the overlay — completing the gesture a keeper can see.
think crop_overlay down-maps the source to a Skate grid (HUNK2) and draws the rectangle's OUTLINE over it: span_cells maps image spans to grid cells by down_map's own integer partition (px*cells/size), so the outline lands on the cells that actually show the rectangle's pixels; only border cells wear crop_slot, the interior keeps the picture — a frame, not a fill.
think Placed the module in brushstroke/ (Skate lives there); crop_gesture lives in image/, so added a symlink brushstroke/crop_gesture.rye -> ../image/crop_gesture.rye, matching the qoi/photo_edits/edit_cursor symlink pattern.
think RED on TAME: the symlink pulled image/crop_gesture.rye into the brushstroke scan roster, exposing compound asserts (assert(a and b)) that HUNK60 never scanned (image/ was off-roster). Split every compound assert in BOTH crop_overlay.rye and crop_gesture.rye — a ratchet-on-touch fix. TAME bans clean after.
obs The selftest proves the outline is a drift-free frame: every border cell of a {2,2,4,4} rectangle (12 cells) wears crop_slot, every interior and exterior cell equals a plain down_map cell-for-cell; a one-cell-wide rectangle is all border; a degenerate rectangle refuses NoRect; a too-large grid folds down_map's GridTooLarge through; the overlay rasterizes lit.
obs Two-plus asserts per fn, invariants positive; width exit 0. The crop_gesture ratchet also improves a file already sent in HUNK60 — accrete, never break.
loom witness=hunk_crop_overlay_witness grid=8x8 rect=2,2,4,4 border_cells=12 result=GREEN
